* D: the uA741 at transistor level, +/-15 V
* Source: the 741 circuit of A. S. Sedra and K. C. Smith, Microelectronic Circuits
* (Fig. 10.1 there), as given in the SPICE companion of G. W. Roberts and A. S. Sedra,
* chapter "Analog Integrated Circuits", Fig. 10.2 (deck) and Table 10.1 (device
* parameters, after P. R. Gray and R. G. Meyer, Analysis and Design of Analog
* Integrated Circuits, 1984). Transcribed with the original node numbers; only the
* subcircuit and model names changed. Generic textbook devices: this is the published
* reference circuit, not a characterized chip. No offset-null pins, no input protection.
* pins: inp inn vcc vee out (Q1 base = non-inverting input)
* Bipolar substrates are tied to 26 (vee), the most negative supply (a 3-terminal BJT
* would put its substrate capacitance CJS on node 0, i.e. on circuit ground).
.subckt OPA_UA741 1 2 25 26 22
